						<p class="pTitle">EverQuest Research Study </p>
							<p class=pText>
							I am a master student at the University of Oslo, Department of<br>Informatics in Norway, and I am writing a thesis about Virtual<br>Communities (that is guilds and alliances) and communication. The goal<br>is to design and develop a prototype of a system that will support<br>communication within Virtual Gaming Communities.<br><br>I am performing a research study of guilds in EverQuest, and as a part<br>of it I have created a questionnaire which is based upon the<br>interviews carried out earlier in this study. The purpose of this<br>questionnaire is to get answers to questions that has arised in the<br>interviews, and to gather quantitative material to see (if possible)<br>trends among the players in EverQuest.<br><br>Below is a link to the questionnaire. It consists of around 30<br>questions and it takes about 10 minutes to answer it. I would<br>appreciate if you could spare the time to fill in the<br>questionnaire. If it is possible, please give the link to other<br>EverQuest players since I rely on getting as many participants as<br>possible.<br><br>The link to the questionnaire is :<br>    http://everquestsurvey.ragnarok.no/index.php<br><br>For more information about this research study, please visit<br>http://ragnarok.no/~johanyg/hfag/<br><br>If you have any questions or thoughts/ideas to this reseach study,<br>please send me an email (johanyg@ragnarok.no).<br><br>Regards,<br><br>Johan Grasmo<br>
							<br>
							 - Johan Grasmo<BR><BR>
