						<p class="pTitle">Geforce 2MX mystery SOLVED!!!  </p>
							<p class=pText>
							For those of us who have a Geforce 2 card, the biggest problem i have been hearing about is the framerate being extremely choppy or slow.  I too have had this dilemma and appear to have solved it.  This may not work for a few of you, but it should work for most.<BR><BR>The biggest problem, especially with AGP videocards is the IRQ sharing problem.  But this is a quick and easy fix if you put your sound card in the top PCI slot and the modem or ehternet card in the PCI slot below that.  I know that on Win 98, The video card and sound card were in IRQ 5, and the ehternet card or modem is on IRQ 11.  This works much better than having everything set up on IRQ 11.  Give it a try!!! <BR><BR>Another issue is that people install DX 8.1 AFTER installing the new video driver.  The problem with this is the fact that DX 8.1 overwrites some of the video drivers with less efficient ones.  Be sure to install the video driver AFTER installing DX 8.1 first!!<BR><BR>That is all...<BR>
							<br>
							 - Calenon<BR><BR>
							</p>
							&nbsp; <a class="abody" href="comments.asp?Index=203">[View Comments]</a>
					
					
