						<p class="pDate">Wednesday, September 19, 2001</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Memorial Event on September 23 </p>
							<p class=pText>
							To All the Guilds of Solusek Ro:<br><br>We hope you will join us in an all-EQ-servers Memorial First Aid Camp on Sunday, September 23rd, at noon PST, as we remember those we lost on September 11th.<br><br>Who are we?  We are an Everquest guild on Morell-Thule, called Random Acts (of kindness).  Twice monthly we give a First Aid Camp for Everquest players, offering free assistance to all players in a particular zone:  buffs, heals, binds, combat assistance, food and drink.  Sometimes we give away the extra items we have picked up in our travels throughout Norrath, provided they are level-appropriate for the zone.<br><br>The effect of these events:  players feel they are not alone in Norrath, because other people care about their welfare.  And isn't that really what counts the most, no matter what world you are in?<br><br>We know we aren't the only ones in Everquest who like to help others; all over Norrath we see the kindness and generosity of players.  That is why we are asking you and members of your guild to join us on this very special day of remembrance: it is an opportunity for all of us to spread kindness, support, and healing in the wake of last week's terrible tragedy.<br><br>This type of event is easy to organize and costs nothing but time.  You can set up a buffing station in a zone where your guild currently likes to congregate, or head to a newbie starting zone with some food, drink, and maybe some level-appropriate items a newbie would greatly appreciate, like low-end weapons and patchwork armor.  Whatever you choose, remember, it's the thought that counts.<br><br>If you have questions, or need assistance setting up an event for your guild, please feel free to contact us at eqrandomacts@hotmail.com, or see our Events, Hunting, and Gathering board at http://pub76.ezboard.com/brandomacts.<br><br>Please join us as we offer our thoughts and hopes to the victims, their families, and their friends at this difficult time.<br><br>On behalf of Random Acts of Morell-Thule,<br><br>Gwion Llewellyn, Random Acts Events Coordinator<br>Hamadryad Long, Guild Founder<br>http://www.eqrandomacts.com<br>eqrandomacts@hotmail.com
							<br>
							 - Random Acts<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
