						<p class="pTitle">RPGwear.com News Release </p>
							<p class=pText>
							-------------------<br><br>RPGwear, an officially licensed provider of EverQuest apparel, is pleased to<br>announce a partnership with Blair Grafix.<br><br>Blair Grafix, a team of renowned artists commissioned by the film industry<br>for its artwork, will work with RPGwear to produce high quality artwork to<br>be featured on RPGwear products. Blair Grafix is well-known for work such as<br>Elf Lord, Elf Quest, Sno, Dick Sweenie, and countless other projects during<br>the past 30 years. Barry Blair, the owner of Blair Grafix, says "We are<br>looking forward to this joint venture."<br><br>The first combined efforts of Blair Grafix and RPGwear have resulted in a<br>design that will be featured on the event shirt for the upcoming EverQuest<br>Fan Faire in San Diego. In addition, RPGwear is releasing the "Druid" shirt,<br>the first in a series of 14 class-related shirts, and will begin offering<br>several new posters featuring Blair Grafix artwork.<br><br>"We are very excited to have Barry and his team on our side. Their work is<br>very stunning and I think it meets the quality of work we produce. I invite<br>you to stop by and see for yourself, I am sure you will agree as I do that<br>they are masters at doing something they love." says Cory Rafiner, President<br>and CEO of RPG Inc.<br><br>RPGwear will be offering its merchandise at the Fan Faire in San Diego. Make<br>sure you stop by and talk with the staff and share your thoughts and ideas.<br><br>These designs along with many others are available at www.RPGwear.com. <br><br>RPG, Inc.<br><br>-----------------<br><br>
							<br>
							 - Be0wulf@rpgwear.com<BR><BR>
							</p>
							
					
