						<p class="pDate">Thursday, August 17, 2000</p>
						<p class="pTitle">Enchanted Circle Guild Event </p>
							<p class=pText>
							Hail one and all... the denizens of Norrath!<br><br><br><br>The Enchanted Cicrle Guild of Solusek Ro is holding an event this Sunday at 10am PST in the Crushbone and Butcherblock zones for its members and freinds of the Enchanted Circle.  Please be aware that we will be in the Crushbone zone for approximately 2 hours hunting slavers and ultimately will result in tackling Emporer Crush himself.  The officers of the Enchanted Circle will be leading 5 goups in this event and we have limited positions available for each group (each group consists of 5 players and one officer).  Below is a letter to my officers regarding the event.  Have a great day and may your adventures be fun and fruitfull.<br><br><br><br>Hablur the Happy Enchanter <br><br>Crown - Solusek Ro<br><br>http://solusekro.homeip.net/solusek<br><br><br><br>GUILD EVENT WHEN: August 20, 2000<br>TIME: 10:00 a.m. PST WHERE: Crushbone and points beyond <br><br><br><br>BACKGROUND <br><br><br><br>Letter from the Crown to all officers: <br><br><br><br>As Professor Mujahid has pointed out there has been a constant stirring of trouble from the Crushbone Orcs. I have decreed that I can no longer have Professor Mujahid sending out singular agents to address this affair. I will outline the events that have recently occurred causing me to take direct action. <br><br><br><br>Up until recently we believed that Emporer Crush has been behind these attacks on our trade that has been directly affecting the agents of the Enchanted Circle. I have learned that this is only partially the case. He is but a pawn in the struggle for power across Norrath. <br><br><br><br>With the recent discovery of Kunark there has been an odd influx in the gem trade approaching from the Dwarven reaches of the Burtcherblock Mountains. What was odd was that unique gems were being reportedly being found in this region. While I am no gemologist, I consulted with the experts in Neriak and was informed that the gems could not have come from the Butcher block Mountains. <br><br><br><br>Now you may all have wondered why I have been in the Fedwyr region for the past week or so. This is the reason. My abilities have come into play and I was able to directly find out that the Gnomes of Steamfont have been paying lower tariffs to the Dwarves for gems and that the standard gems that are available to us, yet unavailable to them except through our trade, are miraculously appearing in the Gnomish Gem Shops. It appears as if a conspiracy is afoot. Furthermore, there are certain Dwarves that are allowing the Orc Runner through the Butcherblock region unmolested. After attacking one and striping his mind of all thought, making him my personal pet for a brief time, I learned the following critical information: The Crushbone Orcs have allied themselves with the Lizards of Kunark and are seeking to gather gems of power for a massive right which will enable the Orcs to desist relations with the Dark Elves of Neriak. Both the Lizards and the Orcs are paying off the corrupt Dwarves with gems and the Gnomes are acting as the selling point. Quite the sordid affair I must say. <br><br><br><br>What I can say is that from this point on I know very little about the motives and import this has to the Lizards of Kunark but it may be possible it has something to do with the captured Elven Princess. I really cannot say until such time as we get agents to Kunark on a regular basis. <br><br><br><br>I have learned recently, from a friend of mine who is an advisor to the Emissary to the Crushbone Orcs, that the Emissary may be receiving funds from Emperor Crush if he will but supply him with victims for this upcoming ritual. He also told me that they are holding many prisoners in the clan holding of the Orcs. Many of them are our allies. <br><br><br><br>I can tolerate this no longer because these actions violate the tenuous balance which we have sought to retain amongst the various factions involved in the Gem Trade. There is more to this than the Gem Trade, but that is not my concern. I do take concern and ownership, that as the holders of knowledge, we are the only ones that can act on this. This matter can not be entrusted to the elves as they are in deep hated of me, nor will the Neriak Dark Elves aid us without starting a race war. <br><br><br><br>Assemble my captains all your men and women for the Enchanted Circle goes on the march! Assemble the Guards and Defenders to smash and fling ether at the foe while I will assemble the beguilers to fear them to their very souls. We march first to free all of our friends, allies and associates from the slave pens in Crushbone then we will directly attack and fell Emporer Crush himself. Should the Emissary be in the midst then he too shall fall for his audacity in directly effecting our affairs in the world. <br><br><br><br>After we have taken Crushbone by force I will assemble the champions of the Enchanted Circle unto me and we will tarry directly to Butcherblock. We will strike before word of the Crushbone fall reaches the treacherous Dwarves. I will leave the Gnomes as warning that the might of the Enchanted Circle is not to be trifled with and that mercy is the only thing that stayed my hand! The Kunark Lizards yet remain out of our realm… but that is only a matter of time… <br><br><br>
							<br>
							 - Hablur<BR><BR>
							</p>
